  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The ugliness of a string is defined as the count of two consecutive ones i.e. `\"11\"` in the given string. For example, the ugliness of string `\"10111\"` is 222.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of NNN integers and you have to find any ordering of the array such that the ugliness of the concatenated string of the binary representations of the integers (without leading zeros) is minimum.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Subtasks"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains an integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. Then TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, output an ordering of AAA such that the ugliness of the array is minimum. If there are multiple answers, you may output any.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 \n3\n3 6 5\n2\n7 6",
        "output": "5 6 3\n6 7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: The binary representations of [5,6,3][5, 6, 3][5,6,3] are [101,110,11][101, 110, 11][101,110,11] and the concatenated string would be \"10111011\" which has ugliness 333. This is the minimum possible. [6,5,3][6, 5, 3][6,5,3] is also valid.\nTest Case 2: The binary representations of [6,7][6, 7][6,7] are [110,111][110, 111][110,111] and the concatenated string would be \"110111\" which has ugliness of 333. This is the minimum possible. [7,6][7, 6][7,6] is not valid as it has ugliness of 444."
      }
    ]
  },
